<% content_for :title, "About — Printwright" %>
<div class="container" style="max-width: 720px">
  <h1>About Printwright</h1>
  <p class="t-small muted"><strong>Testnet build</strong> — this is a working demonstration on
    Hedera testnet, not a production marketplace. Settlements are real testnet transactions;
    the tokens have no monetary value.</p>

  <h2>The problem</h2>
  <p>Conventional 3D-model sales often leave rights in an invoice or account-bound download.
    Printwright explores a machine-readable alternative in which software can discover an offer,
    authorize a bounded payment, receive the files, and retain portable evidence of the licence.</p>

  <h2>What Printwright is</h2>
  <p>A marketplace for <strong>licensed</strong> 3D-printable models. Designers upload a model
    and set licence prices; buyers — human or software agent — pay for a licence over
    <a class="mono" href="<%= Hedera::Network.mirror_base %>/api/v1/network/nodes">Hedera <%= Hedera::Network.name %></a>
    using the x402 protocol. Each real delivery returns a private proof bundle and asynchronously
    anchors only its opaque commitment on Hedera Consensus Service. A holder can disclose the
    bundle so another party can recompute it and compare it with the exact public Mirror Node
    message.</p>

  <h2>How the certificate rail works</h2>
  <p>Each licence offer carries a price and terms. After paid delivery, a retrying job submits an
    opaque commitment envelope to an HCS topic — id
    <a class="mono" href="<%= Hedera::Network.hcs_topic_url %>"><%= Hedera::Network.hcs_topic_id %></a>
    — without publishing the certificate, model, buyer, terms, or transaction. Consensus ordering
    fixes that commitment at a topic position. Verification requires the holder's disclosed proof
    bundle; the verifier recomputes it locally and compares it with the exact Mirror Node message.</p>

  <h2>Three doors, one marketplace</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Agents</strong> — REST + x402 over plain HTTP, no account or API key. See the
      <%= link_to "API docs", docs_path %>.</li>
    <li><strong>Humans</strong> — this storefront, with a wallet as the signer.</li>
    <li><strong>Shopkeeper chat</strong> — search and buy in conversation on this site, the
      first consumer of the agent API.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Project status</h2>
  <p>Printwright runs today on Hedera testnet (HBAR and native USDC). It is a hackathon-stage
    build: functional end to end, not yet audited, and not a claim of production readiness or
    real revenue.</p>
</div>
